  "government": "National/ACT/New Zealand First Coalition Government",
  "content": "\u003cdiv class=\"field field-name-field-government\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"taxonomy-term taxonomy-term--type-government taxonomy-term--view-mode-strapline ds-1col clearfix\"\u003e\n\n  \n\n      \n      \u003cem class=\"archive-indicator\"\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\n      \n  \n\n\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n    \n      \u003ctime class=\"meta meta__date\" datetime=\"\"\u003e\u003ctime datetime=\"2024-02-08T23:22:57Z\"\u003e9 February 2024\u003c/time\u003e\n\u003c/time\u003e\n      \n  \n\n\n  \u003ch1 class=\"article__title\"\u003e\n  New diplomatic appointments\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\n    \n            \u003cul class=\"meta--ministers\"\u003e\n            \u003cli\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"teaser--small minister taxonomy-term taxonomy-term--type-ministers taxonomy-term--view-mode-teaser-small ds-1col clearfix\"\u003e\n\n  \n\n  \u003ca href=\"/minister/rt-hon-winston-peters\" class=\"field-group-link minister__link\" hreflang=\"en\"\u003e    \n      \u003cdiv class=\"field minister__portrait\"\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\n  \n  \n            \u003cdiv class=\"field field--name-field-media-image field--type-image field--label-hidden field--item\"\u003e  \u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/sites/default/files/styles/thumbnail/public/2023-12/Peters.png?itok=Uk86zxEs\" width=\"100\" height=\"100\" alt=\"Winston Peters portrait\" class=\"img-responsive\"/\u003e\n\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n      \n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n      \n  \n\n    \n      \u003cdiv class=\"field minister__title\"\u003e  Rt Hon Winston Peters\n\u003c/div\u003e\n      \n  \n\n\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003c/li\u003e\n      \n      \u003c/ul\u003e\n  \n\n    \n      \u003cem class=\"tag tag--portfolio\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"tag taxonomy-term taxonomy-term--type-portfolios taxonomy-term--view-mode-teaser-small ds-1col clearfix\"\u003e\n\n  \n\n  \n    \u003ca href=\"/portfolio/nationalactnew-zealand-first-coalition-government-2023-2026/foreign-affairs\" hreflang=\"en\"\u003eForeign Affairs\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003c/em\u003e\n      \n  \n\n\n            \u003cdiv class=\"prose field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field--item\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eForeign Minister Winston Peters has today announced five new diplomatic appointments. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u0026#34;Strong and effective diplomacy to protect and advance our interests in the world is needed now more than ever,\u0026#34; Mr Peters says. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003e“We are delighted to appoint senior diplomats from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade to these important roles.”\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe appointments are:\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMark Gibb\u003c/strong\u003e as High Commissioner to Niue.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePhil Hewitt\u003c/strong\u003e as High Commissioner to South Africa.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHelen Tunnah\u003c/strong\u003e as Ambassador to Timor-Leste. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCaroline Beresford\u003c/strong\u003e as Ambassador to Viet Nam. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePaula Wilson\u003c/strong\u003e as Ambassador for Counterterrorism - based in Wellington. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n      ",
  "content_text": "Foreign Minister Winston Peters has today announced five new diplomatic appointments.  \"Strong and effective diplomacy to protect and advance our interests in the world is needed now more than ever,\" Mr Peters says.  “We are delighted to appoint senior diplomats from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade to these important roles.” The appointments are: Mark Gibb as High Commissioner to Niue. Phil Hewitt as High Commissioner to South Africa. Helen Tunnah as Ambassador to Timor-Leste.  Caroline Beresford as Ambassador to Viet Nam.  Paula Wilson as Ambassador for Counterterrorism - based in Wellington.",
  "attachments": null,
